# Flutter index.html Protection

## Rule

The file `/var/www/sovereignsanctuary-web/index.html` is the **Flutter web app bootstrap** (≈1.5KB). It loads `flutter_bootstrap.js` which loads `main.dart.js` — this is the client gateway at `app.sovereignsanctuary.net` with the 3 role buttons (Client, Coach, Admin).

**NEVER overwrite this file** with a dashboard HTML page (e.g., Sovereign Command login, `command.html`, `skyeye.html`).

## What Goes Where

| Directory | `index.html` purpose | Size |
|---|---|---|
| `/var/www/sovereignsanctuary-web/` | Flutter app bootstrap (role chooser gateway) | ~1.5KB |
| `/var/www/sovereign-command/` | Sovereign Command admin login page | ~37KB |

## How This Breaks

Dashboard deploy scripts that copy `*.html` files to `/var/www/sovereignsanctuary-web/` can accidentally overwrite `index.html` if a dashboard page is named (or renamed to) `index.html`. When this happens, `app.sovereignsanctuary.net` shows the admin login instead of the Flutter app — clients and coaches cannot log in.

## Deploy Safeguards

1. **Never `rsync --delete`** dashboard HTML into `/var/www/sovereignsanctuary-web/` — this is already covered by `deployment-safety.mdc`
2. **Never copy `command.html` as `index.html`** into the app web root
3. **After any dashboard deploy**, verify: `grep 'flutter_bootstrap' /var/www/sovereignsanctuary-web/index.html` — must match
4. **After any Flutter build deploy**, the build's own `index.html` (from `mobile/build/web/`) is the correct file to place there
5. **If `index.html` is >5KB** in `/var/www/sovereignsanctuary-web/`, it's wrong — the Flutter bootstrap is ~1.5KB

## Recovery

```bash
# Restore from Flutter build:
cp /opt/clinical-sovereignty-lab/mobile/build/web/index.html /var/www/sovereignsanctuary-web/index.html
```
